repository-code: "https://github.com/laputski/causa-rag"
abstract: >-
  A diagnostic bench for retrieval-augmented generation. It scores every
  question in a golden set separately — retrieval recall and precision, answer
  similarity, whether the answer is grounded in the source it cites, and whether
  a question that should have been refused was — then names the pipeline stage
  that failed, deciding retrieval, reranking or generation from the run's own
  trace. Two runs are compared question by question, so the blast radius of a
  configuration change is visible rather than assumed, and a reviewer's free-text
  comment becomes a classified diagnosis and a reusable golden question. Any RAG
  can connect over a versioned HTTP contract, and diagnostic depth follows what
  that system reports about itself. No document, question or answer leaves the
  host it runs on. Version 0.2.0 adds the first Configuration Report, measured
  on the MIRACL benchmark over 4947 questions in Arabic, Russian and English.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - evaluation
  - regression testing
  - information retrieval
  - root cause analysis
  - local-first
